ata-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li><li><span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c10-t4-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> Energy will become more affordable.</li></ul><p><strong>The Environment</strong></p><ul><li>Nano-robots could rebuild the ozone layer.</li><li>Pollutants such as <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c10-t4-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> could be removed from water</li><li>There will be no <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c10-t4-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> from manufacturing.</li></ul><p><strong>Health and Medicine</strong></p><ul><li>New methods of food production could eradicate famine.</li><li>Analysis of medical <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c10-t4-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;will be speeded up.</li><li>Life expectancy could be increased.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":7}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/cambridge-ielts-10-academic-listening-4-audio-4.mp3"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-c10-t4-l-q1","part_id":"en-c10-t4-l-p1","group_id":"en-c10-t4-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"Pargetter","correct_answer_variants":["Pargetter"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[1],"sourceI